  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA consisting of NNN integers.\n\nFind the number of subsequences SSS having length MMM such that:\n\n\nMMM &gt;\\gt&gt; 111;\nFor any pair of indices (i,j)(i,j)(i,j) in the subsequence SSS, (lcm(M,Si)−Si)=(lcm(M,Sj)−Sj)(lcm(M, S_i) - S_i) = (lcm(M, S_j) - S_j)(lcm(M,Si​)−Si​)=(lcm(M,Sj​)−Sj​). Here lcm(a,b)lcm(a,b)lcm(a,b) denotes the lcm of integers aaa and bbb.\nSince the answer can be huge, print it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\nNote that, a subsequence of an array is obtained by deleting the elements at some (possibly none or all) indices of the array. For example, all the subsequences of array [1,2,2][1, 2, 2][1,2,2] are {[A1],[A2],[A3],[A1,A2],[A1,A3],[A2,A3],[A1,A2,A3]}\\{ [A_1], [A_2], [A_3], [A_1, A_2], [A_1, A_3], [A_2, A_3], [A_1, A_2, A_3] \\}{[A1​],[A2​],[A3​],[A1​,A2​],[A1​,A3​],[A2​,A3​],[A1​,A2​,A3​]}, that is, {[1],[2],[2],[1,2],[1,2],[2,2],[1,2,2]}\\{ [1], [2], [2], [1, 2], [1, 2], [2, 2], [1, 2, 2] \\}{[1],[2],[2],[1,2],[1,2],[2,2],[1,2,2]}.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains TTT, the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, the number of elements in the array.\nThe next line of each test case contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer denoting the answer modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1071 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^71≤Ai​≤107",
      "Sum of NNN of over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 3\n3\n2 2 2\n5\n2 2 3 3 3",
        "output": "0\n4\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There is no subsequence satisfying all the conditions.\n\n\nTest case 222: The valid subsequences are: {A1,A2},{A1,A3},{A2,A3},\\{A_1, A_2\\}, \\{A_1, A_3\\}, \\{A_2, A_3\\},{A1​,A2​},{A1​,A3​},{A2​,A3​}, and {A1,A2,A3}.\\{A_1, A_2, A_3\\}.{A1​,A2​,A3​}.\nFor subsequence {A1,A3}\\{A_1, A_3\\}{A1​,A3​}, (lcm(2,A1)−A1)=(lcm(2,A3)−A3)=0(lcm(2, A_1) - A_1) = (lcm(2, A_3) - A_3) = 0(lcm(2,A1​)−A1​)=(lcm(2,A3​)−A3​)=0.\nSimilarly, for all pairs in the subsequence {A1,A2,A3}\\{A_1, A_2, A_3\\}{A1​,A2​,A3​}, (lcm(3,Si)−Si)=(lcm(3,Sj)−Sj)=4(lcm(3, S_i) -S_i) = (lcm(3, S_j) - S_j) = 4(lcm(3,Si​)−Si​)=(lcm(3,Sj​)−Sj​)=4.\n\n\nTest case 333: The valid subsequences are: {A1,A2},{A3,A4},{A4,A5},{A3,A5},\\{A_1, A_2\\}, \\{A_3, A_4\\}, \\{A_4, A_5\\}, \\{A_3, A_5\\},{A1​,A2​},{A3​,A4​},{A4​,A5​},{A3​,A5​}, and {A3,A4,A5}.\\{A_3, A_4, A_5\\}.{A3​,A4​,A5​}.\nFor subsequence {A1,A2}\\{A_1, A_2\\}{A1​,A2​}, (lcm(2,A1)−A1)=(lcm(2,A2)−A2)(lcm(2, A_1) - A_1) = (lcm(2, A_2) - A_2)(lcm(2,A1​)−A1​)=(lcm(2,A2​)−A2​).  Same condition holds for subsequences {A3,A4},{A4,A5},{A3,A5}\\{A_3, A_4\\}, \\{A_4, A_5\\}, \\{A_3, A_5\\}{A3​,A4​},{A4​,A5​},{A3​,A5​}.\nFor all pairs in the subsequence {A3,A4,A5}\\{A_3, A_4, A_5\\}{A3​,A4​,A5​}, (lcm(3,Si)−Si)=(lcm(3,Sj)−Sj)=0(lcm(3, S_i) -S_i) = (lcm(3, S_j) - S_j) = 0(lcm(3,Si​)−Si​)=(lcm(3,Sj​)−Sj​)=0."
      }
    ]
  },
